# CQRS Pattern for Spring Boot BFF

> **Note:** This BFF project orchestrates HTTP calls to backend services and does NOT use database transactions.
> Therefore, `@Transactional` annotations are NOT used in handlers.

## Core Interfaces (Located in `application/cqrs/`)

```java
// Marker interface for commands (write operations)
public interface Command<T> {}

// Marker interface for queries (read operations)
public interface Query<T> {}

// Command handler
public interface CommandHandler<C extends Command<T>, T> {
    T handle(C command);
}

// Query handler
public interface QueryHandler<Q extends Query<T>, T> {
    T handle(Q query);
}

// Dispatcher interface
public interface Dispatcher {
    <T> T dispatch(Command<T> command);
    <T> T dispatch(Query<T> query);
}
```

## SimpleDispatcher Implementation

```java
@Service
public class SimpleDispatcher implements Dispatcher {
    
    private final ApplicationContext context;
    
    public SimpleDispatcher(ApplicationContext context) {
        this.context = context;
    }
    
    @Override
    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    public <T> T dispatch(Command<T> command) {
        var handlerType = getHandlerType(CommandHandler.class, command.getClass());
        var handler = (CommandHandler<Command<T>, T>) context.getBean(handlerType);
        return handler.handle(command);
    }
    
    @Override
    @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
    public <T> T dispatch(Query<T> query) {
        var handlerType = getHandlerType(QueryHandler.class, query.getClass());
        var handler = (QueryHandler<Query<T>, T>) context.getBean(handlerType);
        return handler.handle(query);
    }
    
    private Class<?> getHandlerType(Class<?> handlerInterface, Class<?> messageType) {
        // Finds handler bean by matching generic type parameter
        return context.getBeansOfType(handlerInterface).values().stream()
            .map(Object::getClass)
            .filter(type -> matchesMessageType(type, handlerInterface, messageType))
            .findFirst()
            .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalStateException(
                "No handler found for " + messageType.getSimpleName()));
    }
}
```

## Query Pattern

```java
// Query record (in application/features/{feature}/{flow}/)
public record SearchContainersQuery(
    ExternalApiProvider backend,
    String containerNumber,
    TradeType tradeType
) implements Query<Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>>> {
    
    public static SearchContainersQuery fromCode(
            ExternalApiProvider backend, 
            String containerNumber, 
            String tradeTypeCode) {
        return new SearchContainersQuery(
            backend,
            containerNumber,
            TradeType.fromCodeOrDefault(tradeTypeCode)
        );
    }
}

// Query handler
@Slf4j
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class SearchContainersQueryHandler 
        implements QueryHandler<SearchContainersQuery, Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>>> {
    
    private final Map<ExternalApiProvider, ContainerSearchStrategy> strategies;
    
    @Override
    public Result<List<ContainerSearchResult>> handle(SearchContainersQuery query) {
        var strategy = strategies.get(query.backend());
        
        if (strategy == null) {
            return Result.failure(DomainErrors.UNSUPPORTED_BACKEND);
        }
        
        log.debug("Executing container search: backend={}, container={}", 
            query.backend(), query.containerNumber());
        
        return strategy.search(query.containerNumber(), query.tradeType());
    }
}
```

## Command Pattern

```java
// Command record
public record RefreshTokenCommand(
    String refreshToken
) implements Command<Result<TokenResult>> {}

// Command handler - orchestrates HTTP calls to backend
@Slf4j
@Service
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class RefreshTokenCommandHandler 
        implements CommandHandler<RefreshTokenCommand, Result<TokenResult>> {
    
    private final KeycloakAuthPort keycloakAuthPort;
    
    @Override
    public Result<TokenResult> handle(RefreshTokenCommand command) {
        log.debug("Refreshing token");
        
        return keycloakAuthPort.refreshToken(command.refreshToken());
    }
}
```

## Result Pattern Integration

All handlers MUST return `Result<T>` types:

```java
// Success case
return Result.success(new TokenResult(accessToken, refreshToken, expiresIn));

// Failure case  
return Result.failure(DomainErrors.TOKEN_REFRESH_FAILED);

// From error code and message
return Result.failure("Backend.Unavailable", "Backend service is unavailable");
```

## Controller Integration (Mandatory Pattern)

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/bff/containers")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ContainerSearchController {
    
    // ONLY dependency is Dispatcher - enforced by ArchUnit
    private final Dispatcher dispatcher;
    
    @GetMapping("/search/{backend}")
    public ResponseEntity<ContainerSearchResponse> search(
            @PathVariable ExternalApiProvider backend,
            @RequestParam("q") @ValidContainerNumber String rawContainerNumber,
            @RequestParam(value = "tradeType", defaultValue = "I") String tradeTypeCode) {
        
        // 1. Sanitize input
        var containerNumber = InputSanitizer.sanitizeContainerNumber(rawContainerNumber);
        
        // 2. Create query
        var query = SearchContainersQuery.fromCode(backend, containerNumber, tradeTypeCode);
        
        // 3. Dispatch and handle result
        var results = dispatcher.dispatch(query)
            .getOrThrow(error -> new DomainErrorException(error, mapErrorToHttpStatus(error)));
        
        // 4. Map to response DTO
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ContainerSearchResponse.fromApplication(results));
    }
    
    private HttpStatus mapErrorToHttpStatus(Error error) {
        return switch (error.code()) {
            case "Backend.Unsupported" -> HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST;
            case "Container.NotFound" -> HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND;
            case "Backend.ServiceUnavailable" -> HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE;
            default -> HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR;
        };
    }
}
```

## Controller Constraints (MANDATORY - Enforced by ArchUnit)

### What Controllers CAN Do

- Inject `Dispatcher` as the ONLY application layer dependency
- Create Command/Query records from request DTOs
- Call `dispatcher.dispatch(command)` or `dispatcher.dispatch(query)`
- Map application results to web response DTOs
- Handle HTTP-specific concerns (request parsing, response building, status codes)
- Sanitize input using `InputSanitizer`

### What Controllers CANNOT Do

| Violation | Why It's Wrong |
|-----------|---------------|
| Inject `*Handler` directly | Bypasses dispatcher, couples controller to specific handlers |
| Inject `*Port` interfaces | Business logic belongs in handlers, not controllers |
| Inject `*Client` (HTTP clients) | HTTP calls to backends belong in handlers or adapters |
| Inject `RestClient` | Same as above - no direct HTTP client usage |
| Contain business logic | Controllers are thin - dispatch and transform only |

### ArchUnit Enforcement

These constraints are enforced at build time by `CleanArchitectureTest.java`:

```java
@ArchTest
static final ArchRule controllers_should_not_depend_on_query_handlers = noClasses()
    .that().resideInAPackage("..web.controller..")
    .and().haveSimpleNameEndingWith("Controller")
    .should().dependOnClassesThat().haveSimpleNameEndingWith("QueryHandler");

@ArchTest
static final ArchRule controllers_should_not_depend_on_command_handlers = noClasses()
    .that().resideInAPackage("..web.controller..")
    .and().haveSimpleNameEndingWith("Controller")
    .should().dependOnClassesThat().haveSimpleNameEndingWith("CommandHandler");

@ArchTest
static final ArchRule controllers_should_not_depend_on_application_ports = noClasses()
    .that().resideInAPackage("..web.controller..")
    .and().haveSimpleNameEndingWith("Controller")
    .should().dependOnClassesThat().haveSimpleNameEndingWith("Port");
```

