**Rules:**
- Classes MUST be in flow-based sub-packages (e.g., `auth.token`, NOT directly in `auth`)
- Port interfaces MUST be in `common/` sub-packages
- Features MUST NOT depend on each other
- All records MUST be top-level classes (not nested)

## Conventions

- Commands MUST return `Result<T>` (with value) or `Result<Void>` (without value)
- Queries MUST return `Result<T>` with DTOs
- Use records for commands, queries, and results
- ONE handler per command/query
- Handlers are Spring `@Service` components
- **NO `@Transactional` annotations** - this BFF orchestrates HTTP calls, not database operations
- **Controllers MUST only depend on `Dispatcher`** - enforced by ArchUnit

**See also:** `bff-architecture.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`, `http-clients.mdc`
